Our greetings to the people of Oljiyo as well.

142
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Em pir vî derî hatine masiya.
 
We have come here a lot for fishing.

143
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Em di ber re diçûn Sêbîdarê...
 
We used to go past here to Sebîdar...

144
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Devera Mexoberd... Tualîsêt...
 
The area of Mexoberd... Tualîsêt...

145
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Vê de digot Gulê Nebî em diçûn masiya.
 
Here, it was called Gulê Nebî, we went fishing.

146
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Ewa gundê Pengû ye.
 
That is Pengu's village.

147
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Noka emê gundî... gundî jî we re darxin.
 
Now we will show the village... show the village to you.

148
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Cem gundê Qenet jî heye.
 
There is also Qenet near the village.

149
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
Erê hevalno li vê derê jî...
 
Yes friends, here as well...

150
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Ewa me got gundê Oljiyo ye.
 
That which we said is Oljiyo village.

151
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Erê Pengû ewa gundê te ye.
 
Yes Pengu, that is your village.

152
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Te berê vî jî ji me xwestibû.
 
You had asked for this from us before.

153
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Ha va gundê we ye.
 
Here is your village.

154
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,000
Erê milet ji me xwest.
 
Yes, the people asked us.

155
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Birakî me Pengû jî ji me xwestibû gundê Oljiyo...
 
Our brother Pengu also asked us for Oljiyo village...

156
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
...em we re bişewirînin.
 
...for us to film it for you.

157
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:13,000
Ha va divê geçê va me got em bişewirînin.
 
Here at this crossing we said let's film.

158
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Noka em man geçê din va jî bişewirînin.
 
Now we are left to film the other crossing too.

159
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:19,000
Erê a di ber re pir diçû masiya.
 
Yes, the one who used to go fishing past here a lot.

160
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Berê vira av dadihatkî.
 
Before, water used to flow down here.

161
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:23,000
Hevalno vir kanî hebû.
 
Friends, there was a spring here.

162
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Me tam dihat vî derî, vê kaniyê me av jê vedixwar.
 
We used to come exactly here, we drank water from this
spring.

163
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,000
Û em diçûn.
 
And we would go.

164
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Şîşe me ji vir dadigirtin.
 
We filled bottles from here.

165
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Tuzik derdiket.
 
Watercress used to grow.

166
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Miletê vira lê sêrke, ê zane be.
 
The people of here, look at it, they will know.

167
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Erê Pengû gundê te ye...
 
Yes Pengu, it's your village...

168
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Maşallah.
 
Mashallah.

169
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:40,000
Bayê vî derî jî temam e maşallah.
 
The air of this place is also perfect, mashallah.

170
00:28:40,000 --> 00:29:00,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

171
00:29:35,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Erê hevalno li vî derî jî em li gundê Oljiyo ne.
 
Yes friends, here we are also in the village of Oljiyo.

172
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Em cem Abu Salah ne.
 
We are with Abu Salah.

173
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Li vî derî dikanek vekiriye, semon... xizmet dike.
 
He opened a shop here, samoon [bread]... he serves.

174
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Bi vî tûnî her tiştî xizmet dikin.
 
With this oven, they serve everything.

175
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Em dibên seetên te xweş.
 
We say may your hours be pleasant [have a good time].

176
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,000
Me got merhaba apê Xalo.
 
We said hello Uncle.

177
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Ahlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

178
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Xalo gundê... gundê we Oljiyo. Kê nav lê kiriye Oljiyo?
 
Uncle, the village... your village Oljiyo. Who named it
Oljiyo?

179
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Oljiyo bi xwe du nav lê dibên.
 
Oljiyo itself, they say two names for it.

180
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,000
Olci ye.. navê gund.
 
It is Olci... the name of the village.

181
00:30:02,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Nav.. navê gund..
 
The name... the name of the village...

182
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Ol, zmanê Tirkî ye, yê resîg e, ew vederê dido.
 
Ol, in the Turkish language, is "surveyor" (or measurer),
they gave it that [name].

183
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Şêxler bîn, wî wextî gotine mala Ismaîlê Memê.
 
They were Sheikhs, at that time they called it the house of
Ismail Meme.

184
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Mala Ismaîlê Memê.
 
The house of Ismail Meme.

185
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Ismaîlê Memê. Şêxler bîn û xwedan beraq bîn.
 
Ismail Meme. They were Sheikhs and they were flag bearers.

186
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

187
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:17,000
Beraqê şêxliqê ye.
 
It is the flag of Sheikhdom.

188
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

189
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:22,000
Ê diduyê, bi Kurmancî... bi Kurmancî dibê... dibê Olci.
 
Secondly, in Kurmanji... in Kurmanji they say... they say
Olci.

190
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Olci.
 
Olci.

191
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,000
Olci. Ciyê beraqê.
 
Olci. The place of the flag.

192
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Ciyê beraqê. Olci.
 
The place of the flag. Olci.

193
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Ciyê beraqê. Ol, Ol bi Kurmancî beraq e, Ci cî ye. Cî ye,
erê.
 
The place of the flag. "Ol", "Ol" in Kurmanji is flag, "Ci"
is place. It is place, yes.

194
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Saeta te xweş, agahiyên te xweş in. Xolu, çaze hawş li vê
derê heye?
 
Bless you, your information is good. Uncle, how many
households are here?

195
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Teqrîben 65 hawş hene.
 
There are approximately 65 households.

196
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:39,000
65? Maşallah, maşallah. Xolu, sukana xwe gih heye?
 
65? Mashallah, mashallah. Uncle, is its population all here?

197
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Teqrîben 150 hene.
 
Approximately 150 are here.

198
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:44,000
Maşallah, maşallah.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

199
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Vê mantiqê, ewê cem me da, miletê xwe yanî teqrîben gel mal
ne?
 
In this region, here with us, our people are almost all at
home, right?

200
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:53,000
Bes aliyê we varda, ew no tebê, ev milet van nageriyaye, kî
ye ma?
 
But on your side over there, isn't it so, hasn't this nation
returned? Who remains?

201
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Na na, vegeriyane. Hinek hene zivistanê tên ser hawşên xwe
çêdikin, dar dikin.
 
No, no, they have returned. Some come in the winter to fix
their houses, do the trees.

202
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Û berê esas li Helebê bûn.
 
And originally, they were in Aleppo.

203
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

204
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Tek ro derdê nan, Heleb, ser şuxulê xwe û tiyê dinê.
 
Only because of the struggle for bread, Aleppo, for their
work and worldly things.

205
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Eywa. Yanî ne ku ji ber gundî derketin?
 
Yes. So it wasn't that they left because of the village
itself?

206
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:12,000
Na na, ne ku dilê me esil... esil daxwaza me şikandinê
derneketine yanî.
 
No, no, not that our hearts originally... originally we
didn't leave by our own desire to break away.

207
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:13,000
Eywa. Ji ber derneketin.
 
Yes. They didn't leave because of that.

208
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:14,000
Erê, nisbetek pir derneketiye.
 
Yes, a large percentage hasn't left.

209
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Erê. Saeta te xweş.
 
Yes. Bless you.

210
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Xolu, tu çi silavê dişînî ji miletê lavane, ewên dûrî welat,
vanê li me seyr dikin, tu çi silavê dişînî?
 
Uncle, what greetings do you send to the young people, those
far from the homeland, those watching us, what greetings do
you send?

211
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Silavên me ji giyan re heye. Û berî giyan hûn bi xêr hatin û
saeta we xweş.
 
We have greetings for everyone. And before all, welcome to
you and bless you.

212
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Û ê ne li vê derê jî em daxwazin her kes biftile were.
 
And those not here, we wish for everyone to turn back and
come.

213
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:32,000
Ser malên xwe, ser ardê xwe, ser rizqê xwe.
 
To their homes, to their land, to their sustenance.

214
00:31:32,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Liyanî, tu zanî ax bi milet şîrin e. Ax bi milet şîrin e.
 
Because, you know the soil is sweet with [its] people. The
soil is sweet with [its] people.

215
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Û em giştk warê me, em giştk warê me li vê mantiqê da.
 
And we all, our place, we are all locals in this region.

216
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Yanî berî giyan, em bêjin kesê miriyê xwe tînin, tînin, li
giyan tînin.
 
I mean before all, let's say people bring their dead, they
bring them, they bring them to the villages.

217
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Yanî yek meselan bilo xwedê bîne, meselan tirbê, yekî gundî,
bavêk gundî, kalkê gundî li vê derê ne.
 
Meaning one, for example, if God brings it [death], for
example the graves, a villager, a villager's father, a
villager's grandfather are here.

218
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:59,000
Bilo hesabê axê bikin, hesabê miriyê xwe bikin, axa xwe
bikin.
 
Let them consider the soil, consider their dead, consider
their land.

219
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:02,000
Û silavên me ji giyan re heye, biftilin ser axa xwe.
 
And we have greetings to everyone, may they return to their
land.

220
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:07,000
Saeta te xweş Xolu. Tabam xedirê xelkê Olciya, gundekî
gelekî xweş e, gundekî cenet e.
 
Bless you Uncle. Of course, the appreciation of the people
of Olci, it is a very beautiful village, a paradise village.

221
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Cenet e, erê welle.
 
It is paradise, yes by God.

222
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Silavên me ji miletê gundî, ewê rehane... Olciya re.
 
Our greetings to the people of the village, those who are
gone... to [the people of] Olci.

223
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Silavên me ji vê re hene. Çûçik mezin, çavê giyan maç dikim.
 
Our greetings are for them. Small and big, I kiss the eyes
of all.

224
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Niha jî emê jewlekê, ka nava gundî Olciya wara teswîr kin.
Gundî Olciya jî mekû bayê xwe tam heye.
 
Now we will take a tour, come let's film inside the village
of Olci. The village of Olci also has a distinct wind/air.

225
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:23,000
Tam bayê xwe heye.
 
It has a distinct wind/air.

226
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:27,000
Xolu, tu samûn li vir vekirî ye? Şixul hereket heye? Şixul
çû ye?
 
Uncle, is your [shop/business] open here? Is there work
activity? How is the work?

227
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:33,000
Bi xwedê elhemdulîlah, şikr ji xwedê re. Tabam şixulê honakî
bi milet dibe. Her milet hebe şixul çêdibe, derdibe.
 
By God, praise be to God, thanks to God. Of course, work
like this happens with people. Whenever people are present,
work happens, it comes out.

228
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Bi milet tê.
 
It comes with the people.

229
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,000
Xolu, eprat micama, mamoste.
 
Uncle, the apparatus... teacher.

230
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Gotin mamoste...
 
They said teacher...

231
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Vêra dibên Gûla Nebî çiye? Ewa rod bu?
 
They call this place Gula Nebi (Prophet's Flower/Peak)? Was
that it?

232
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:41,000
Gûla Nebî heye. Te xwestî ez ji te re bêjim, tiştekî hebe...
 
There is Gula Nebi. You asked me to tell you, if there is
anything...

233
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Tu ji wan re eprat be, mamoste.
 
Tell them [about] the apparatus, teacher.

234
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:49,000
Gûla Nebî heye. Li vê derê dibên jêrî vê derê, Geliyê Gorûzê
heye.
 
There is Gula Nebi. Here, they say below this place, there
is the Goruz Valley.

235
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,000
Geliyê Gorûzê li hember Olciya ye.
 
The Goruz Valley is opposite Olci.

236
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:57,000
Û di vê derê ortê, gelê ro heye, têkeve meselan di cema
kaniya keş.
 
And here in the middle, there is a valley, it enters for
example near the Priest's Spring (Kaniya Keş).

237
00:32:57,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Xwedê rehma xwe li kaniya keş bike, em bêjin.
 
May God have mercy on the Priest's Spring, let us say.

238
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Kaniya keş.
 
The Priest's Spring.

239
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:04,000
Li cema kaniya hêfis heye, kaniya fês...
 
Near the Hefis Spring, the Fes spring...

240
00:33:04,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Hêfis heye, erê.
 
There is Hefis, yes.

241
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Û ev geliyên berê giştik qewax bûn.
 
And these valleys used to be entirely poplar trees.

242
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:10,000
Giştik qewax bûn?
 
They were entirely poplar trees?

243
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Tabam niha ti.. lo jî bû du sal in, sê sal in belkî kêmîneyê
baranê zara av jî kêm bûye yanî.
 
Of course now noth... even now it has been two years, three
years, perhaps due to the lack of rain, the water has also
decreased.

244
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Av jî kêm e.
 
The water is also scarce.

245
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:28,000
Û kaniyek jî di vê derê de hebû, me vêra digot Kaniya Şirb,
nizanin me bîr kir, me bîr nekir.
 
And there was a spring in here too, we called it the Shirb
Spring, I don't know if we remembered it or not.

246
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:30,000
Ma em tak rûyê hevdu dikin.
 
We are just looking at each other's faces.

247
00:33:30,000 --> 00:33:31,000
Saeta te xweş.
 
Bless you.

248
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Xolu, xwedê ke na Kaniya Akeş di binî vira hebû ye?
 
Uncle, God willing... wasn't the Akesh Spring below here?

249
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Howe, me vêra digo, me vêra digo Kaniya Akeş.
 
Yes, we called it that, we called it the Akesh Spring.

250
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:39,000
Kaniya Akeş. Nanê tîr li ser avê dixwarî, min tûzik jî da
ber.
 
Akesh Spring. Eating thin bread (Nanê tîr) by the water, I
also put cress (tûzik) with it.

251
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Tûzik jî hebû. Erê, belkî min...
 
There was cress too. Yes, maybe I...

252
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Şik bû ye?
 
Was it doubtful?

253
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Erê, tûzik jî hebû. Û kilam jî li ser gelî û ser tûzikê
hebû.
 
Yes, there was cress too. And there were songs about the
valley and about the cress.

254
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:50,000
Hawa jî li Pungur dimîne ji wara wî klamî bibêje, derbike.
 
That remains for Pungur to sing that song for you, to bring
it out.

255
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:53,000
Xolu, tu silavekî bişîne Pungur, mubaşerî ser kê? Bişîne.
 
Uncle, send a greeting to Pungur, directly on who? Send it.

256
00:33:53,000 --> 00:33:57,000
Merheba Pungur, îşê te çawa ye? Halê te çawa ye?
 
Hello Pungur, how is your work? How is your situation?

257
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:04,000
Saeta te xweş, herû meselan ehbabê te, dostê te, em gişta
didin nîzîk, û herû jî me da nîzîk bîne.
 
Bless you, always for example your loved ones, your friends,
we consider everyone close, and always bring us close too.

258
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:07,000
Bîstina gundî te û bîstina gundî me.
 
Hearing of your village and hearing of our village.

259
00:34:07,000 --> 00:34:11,000
Bîstina gundî me. Kêşko zane, ewiya me hebû tu jî vêra ba.
 
Hearing of our village. I wish, you know, we had this [wish]
that you were here too.

260
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:14,000
Û te li ser navê min, te bavê Gîvara jî silav ke. Bavê
Gîvara.
 
And on my behalf, you greet Givara's father too. Givara's
father.

261
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Ewî jî silav ke.
 
Greet him too.

262
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:18,000
Silavên me jî ji wê re hene, bavê Gîvara.
 
Our greetings are to him too, Givara's father.

263
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Û saeta we xweş. Û niha jî emkî herin hewşa wa.
 
And bless you. And now we will go to your courtyards/houses.

264
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Înşalah hewşê jî teswîr bikin û gundî teswîr bikin.
 
God willing, film the courtyards and film the village.

265
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Înşalah.
 
God willing.

266
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:30,000
Û leqatekî heye li hember mala wa, ser Geliyê Çûrtanê jî.
 
And there is a shot opposite your house, over the Churtan
Valley too.

267
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Erê. Ser Geliyê Çûrtanê.
 
Yes. Over the Churtan Valley.

268
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:32,000
Erê, ser Geliyê Çûrtanê.
 
Yes, over the Churtan Valley.

269
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:40,000
Gel mala we rûniştin, yolî wê da, vêra dibên merxê, merxê di
mala cebeli hebû jî, hewê jî velle bike.
 
Sitting with your family, looking that way, they call it the
Juniper, the Juniper in the mountain house was there too, do
that one too, by God.

270
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

271
00:34:41,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Hewê jî velle bike. Lewra cebeli, zane vêra dibê Rehmanê
Weqis, kolî te ye, bi îtîbar mileqeb vêra dibên Cebeli.
 
Do that one too, by God. Because Cebeli, you know they call
him Rehmane Weqis, he is your grandpa/elder, respectfully
nicknamed Cebeli here.

272
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:51,000
Zana dibên Merxê Cebeli, manê wî leqatê jî îştera were. Û
saeta we xweş.
 
You know they say "Cebeli's Juniper", meaning let that shot
come to you too. And bless you.

273
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Serketa te xweş, saet xweş Xolu, xwedê ji te razî be. Xwedê
emrê te dirêj bike de.
 
Good luck to you, bless you Uncle, may God be pleased with
you. May God lengthen your life.

274
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Xolu, qîçikê te li der va hene?
 
Uncle, do you have children abroad?

275
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:55,000
Na, li der va tüne ne.
 
No, none abroad.

276
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Tüne ne? Cem te ne?
 
None? They are with you?

277
00:34:56,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Na, qîçikê min, xwedê we ji wara bihêle, sê lawik in, li cem
min in.
 
No, my children, may God spare yours for you, are three
boys, they are with me.

278
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Û qîzik jî wehîd e, ew jî...
 
And the daughter is the only one, she is also...

279
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Xwedê ji wara bihêle, xwedê destê xwe ser ard bigre.
 
